From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jonathan Schwender <schwenderjonathan@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 04:23:36 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] servoshell: Run the servoshell executable headless on
 OpenHarmony

It renders offscreen, so it can be started from an `hdc shell` without an app,
and several instances can run on one device. `./mach build --ohos
--headless-binary` builds it and puts it into a directory together with the
runtime libraries and resources it needs.

Validation: `./mach build --ohos --release --headless-binary --no-package` stages `servoshell-headless/` with the executable, `libc++.so` and the resources, and `./mach build --ohos --release --no-package` still builds the library of the app. The next two patches ran WPT with the executable from `hdc shell`, with four instances at once on an API 26 HarmonyOS phone and two on a HiHope DAYU200 (OpenHarmony 7.0, API 26).
AI-assisted: Yes (agent session; written by the agent, which also ran the checks above)
Signed-off-by: Jonathan Schwender <schwenderjonathan@gmail.com>
